"""Triton implementation of ``aten::__rshift__``.

A right shift is one ALU op per element, so the operator is entirely
launch-bound: the kernel itself runs in well under a microsecond on the
benchmark shapes while the launch dominates.  The generic
``pointwise_dynamic`` path spent one rank-specialised block-pointer launch
plus the full argument promotion / stride machinery per call.  Flattening to
a single 1-D launch over contiguous storage cuts the 1K-element calls from
~10-17us to ~3.5us (2.7-4x, in line with the native operator) and stays
ahead at 1M-2M elements.  Non-dense, broadcast, mixed-dtype and
mismatched-out calls keep the stride-aware pointwise path.
"""

